		{
			"id": "tiaYHtvv-QJACwsv0",
			"name": "Warp Blast",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Zoanthrope's signature attack: a crackling bolt of raw psychic force hurled from its forehead that burns through armour as readily as flesh — the bioform's entire battlefield purpose across every Codex edition and the reason a Zoanthrope brood is treated as priority artillery in Black Library's Hive Fleet fiction.\n\nDesign: Innate Attack (Burning, 5/die, B61) with Armor Divisor (2) (+50%, B103, matching this project's Necron gauss-tier armour-piercing convention) plus the standard Warp Sorcery/Perils pair, net +20%. Full modified cost: 5 x 1.2 = 6 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "maWs9YChyTyGFBEwB",
					"name": "Armor Divisor (2), +50%",
					"cost_adj": "50%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mk0ScnCkEMQOYHZ0W",
					"name": "Warp Sorcery, -20%",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mIAwGZfyK3bfVp-Cd",
					"name": "Perils of the Warp, -10%",
					"cost_adj": "-10%"
				}
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "tihmahap2bBHqs1UH",
			"name": "Catalyst",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Floods a group of nearby bioforms with the Hive Mind's own regenerative biomass, accelerating wound closure mid-fight — Codex background's explanation for why a synapse creature's brood sometimes shrugs off damage that should have dropped it, and this project's own reasoned scaling of that effect into a named, castable power (no single cited scene names \"Catalyst\" as such; the underlying effect — a Zoanthrope-cast healing buff on nearby Tyranids — is well documented across editions).\n\nDesign: Basic Set Healing (10 points/level, B59) at the leveled rate used throughout this project's own Biomancy entries, with Area Effect (+50%, B102, a squad-wide buff matching this project's own Librarius: Might of Heroes build) plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +20%; scaled to this file's 5/level baseline to keep it in line with the file's other single-target-scale powers rather than a full Basic Healing die-for-die cost. Full modified cost: 5 x 1.2 = 6 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mIjNPodAjW8nVey9f",
					"name": "Area Effect",
					"cost_adj": "+50%"
				},
				{
					"id": "m5IIvVhIyu16XVSLn",
					"name": "Warp Sorcery",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "msyWgQ8Oim6mYp6mq",
					"name": "Perils of the Warp",
					"cost_adj": "-10%"
				}
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "t4S_UalrrY5QDgcc2",
			"name": "The Horror",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A wave of pure, alien wrongness projected directly into a target's mind, distinct from Shadow in the Warp's constant background hum — a focused psychic terror-strike the Hive Mind can direct at a single dangerous enemy (an officer, a Librarian) rather than merely radiating outward. Consistent with Codex background's framing of the Hive Mind as capable of directed as well as ambient psychic effects.\n\nDesign: Terror, Basic's core advantage (flat 30 + 10/level for extra range, B), with Warp Sorcery/Perils, net -30%, identical build to this project's own Telepathy: Terrify entry. Full modified cost: (30+10) x 0.7 = 28 points at its default first extra-range level; needs Warp Empowerment level 2 (cap 30).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "m4Y35jxLyR4yzUZiC",
					"name": "Warp Sorcery",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "m4y-YcguACVTXLskg",
					"name": "Perils of the Warp",
					"cost_adj": "-10%"
				}
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1,
			"base_points": 30
		},
		{
			"id": "t5DrPlLRCT5ejed9K",
			"name": "Dominion",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Hive Tyrant's own signature working: it reaches into a target with the same crushing psychic weight it uses to hold its own swarm together, stripping away whatever protects them and leaving them more vulnerable to everything that follows — Codex background names this kind of debuff among a synapse lord's psychic gifts, and this project's own reasoned scaling of it onto the Hive Mind's known telepathic dominance theme, on the model of this project's Librarius: Null Zone (the closest published analogue for \"strip an enemy's defences from a distance\").\n\nDesign: Affliction (10/level) delivering a Vulnerability-style disadvantage valued at roughly -20 points (+20%, matching this project's own Null Zone valuation), Malediction (+100%, B36), Warp Sorcery and the Severe Perils tier (a Hive Tyrant-scale psychic push, matching Null Zone's own Severe tier), net +80%. Full modified cost: 10 x 1.8 = 18 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 2 (cap 30).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mRw52aR0dakZlUh8O",
					"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Vulnerability x1.5, -20 pts)",
					"cost_adj": "20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mIYrOh9Mjs21DFZUN",
					"name": "Malediction 1",
					"cost_adj": "+100%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mY2ORhxd8a8oqmULr",
					"name": "Warp Sorcery",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				},
				{
					"id": "mwIAaXFjuOcnhLZE6",
					"name": "Perils of the Warp (Severe)",
					"cost_adj": "-20%"
				}
			],
			"points_per_level": 10,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "tJLCBWEXGomixx8Gw",
			"name": "Onslaught",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A burst of psychic urgency that drives a brood of nearby bioforms to move and strike faster than their bodies alone would allow — the Hive Mind's answer to a Librarian's pre-charge blessing, and this project's own reasoned scaling of the well-documented \"the swarm surges forward all at once\" beat into a named, castable power (no single cited scene names \"Onslaught\" specifically).\n\nDesign: Increased Basic Speed (5 points per +0.25, B) with Area Effect (+50%) plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +20%, the same build this project's Ork Warpath: Warp Speed (Mob) entry uses for an equivalent squad-wide speed buff. Full modified cost: 5 x 1.2 = 6 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
