		{
			"id": "tYtw_ubmA7gz87G3I",
			"name": "Paroxysm",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Scrambles a single enemy's senses and coordination from a distance, leaving them stumbling and half-blind for a few crucial seconds — Codex background across editions gives this kind of debilitating single-target effect to Zoanthrope-tier psykers as an alternative to outright blasting a hard target.\n\nDesign: Affliction (10/level) delivering a Blindness/Klutz-style disadvantage valued at roughly -20 points (+20%), Malediction (+100%, B36), plus Warp Sorcery/Perils, net +90%. Full modified cost: 10 x 1.9 = 19 points/level; needs Warp Empowerment level 2 (cap 30) — the same math this project's own Biomancy: Haemorrhage entry uses for an equivalent single-target debuff.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"modifiers": [
				{
					"id": "mbycppR2Su1yZku-6",
					"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Blindness or Klutz, -20 pts)",
